# REVERSED: Early Modern English -> Midlands Middle English
# Source: Index Diachronica 17.7.2.1.4 "Midlands Middle English to Early Modern English",
#   contributed by Pogostick Man, citing FireSpeakerWiki ("English sound changes", 2013).
#   https://chridd.nfshost.com/diachronica/all#Early-Modern-English
# License: CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 (this derived file carries the same license; noncommercial use only).
# STATUS: DRAFT by Claude, awaiting team review.
#
# Forward rules in the source, in its order:
#   E1  ʊ → ɤ ! P_ and _l                              [FOOT-STRUT split]
#   E2  mb ŋɡ → m ŋ / _#
#   E3  tj sj dj zj → tʃ ʃ dʒ ʒ / ! _uː                [yod coalescence]
#   E4  a ɑ {ɛ,ɪ,ɤ} → ɑː ɔː ɜː / _ɹ{C,#}
#   E5  ɑʊ → ɑː / _P
#   E6  ɑʊ → ɑː / _N (sometimes)
#   E7  ɑʊ → ɔː / else
#   (note) many ɑː later became ɔː "for non-phonetic reasons" — not a rule
#   E8  a → ɑː / "in a few words, like 'father'"
#   E9  a → æ / else                                   [TRAP]
#   E10 əɪ əʊ → ɑi æʊ / "in some parts of South-Eastern England"
#   E11 əɪ əʊ → aɪ aʊ / "in most of Britain"
#   E12 eː oː → eɪ oʊ / ! _ɹ
#
# HOW THIS FILE WORKS
# One simultaneous block, as in Midlands-Middle-English.lsc: each Early Modern English sound
# maps straight to its Middle English source, and no output is rewritten again.
#
# REVIEW NOTES
# - E10 is a regional variant; British English follows E11, so only E11 is reversed.
# - E1: modern IPA writes the STRUT vowel ʌ; both ʌ and the source's ɤ reverse to ʊ.
# - E4 reverses only directly before ɹ (r): ɜː branches to ɛ ɪ ʊ, ɔː to ɑ, ɑː to a.
# - E8 ("father") reverses as a branch on every ɑː.
# - Notation bridge (not a sound change): this section writes lax ɪ ɛ ʊ, a and ɹ where the
#   Middle English section writes i e u, ɑ and r.
# - Added by team request (not in the source): the Great Vowel Shift. The source has it
#   in neither this section nor the Middle English one, though E11 starts from its
#   intermediate əɪ əʊ. Forward: iː > əɪ > aɪ, uː > əʊ > aʊ, eː > iː, ɛː > eː > iː,
#   oː > uː, ɔː > oː (> oʊ by E12), ɑː > ɛː > eː (> eɪ by E12). Each modern vowel maps
#   straight to its Middle English source, branching where the Shift merged vowels:
#     iː < eː or ɛː (meet, meat);  eɪ < ɑː or ej (name, day);  oʊ < ɔː, ɔːw or ow;
#     eː before r < ɑː or ɛː;  oː before r < ɔː or oː;
#     ʊ ʌ < u, or < oː shortened after the Shift (foot, blood).
# - Added by team request (not in the source): the loss of x/ç (gh) before t.
#   aɪ before t also branches to ME ih (night < niht); ɔː before t also branches to ME ow,
#   which Midlands-Middle-English.lsc (M10) takes back to OE oh ɑːh oːh (daughter < dohtor).
#   The Index's Middle English writes h for x/ç; Old-English.lsc maps ç x to h anyway.
# - Also missing from the source: the laxing of short i e u to ɪ ɛ ʊ, handled here by the
#   notation bridge.

Symbol ɑː, ɔː, ɜː, eː, oː, iː, uː, ɛː, tʃ, dʒ

Class labial {p, b, f, v, m}
Class nasal {m, n, ŋ}

emode-to-me:
    # E12 + Great Vowel Shift (team): eɪ < eː < ME ɑː (or ME ej); oʊ < oː < ME ɔː (or ɔːw, ow)
    e² ɪ => e j
    e ɪ => ɑː *
    o² ʊ => ɔː w
    o³ ʊ => o w
    o ʊ => ɔː *
    # Lost gh (team): aɪ before t < ME ih
    a² ɪ => i h / _ t
    # E11 + Great Vowel Shift (team): aɪ aʊ < əɪ əʊ < ME iː uː
    a ɪ => iː *
    a ʊ => uː *
    # Great Vowel Shift (team): iː < eː or ɛː; uː < oː; before r, eː < ɑː or ɛː, oː < ɔː or oː
    iː² => ɛː
    iː => eː
    uː => oː
    eː² => ɛː / _ ɹ
    eː => ɑː / _ ɹ
    oː² => oː / _ ɹ
    oː => ɔː / _ ɹ
    # Shortened oː after the Shift (team): foot, blood
    ʊ² => oː
    {ʌ², ɤ²} => oː
    # E5, E6: ɑː < ɑʊ before labials and nasals
    ɑː² => ɑ w / _ @labial
    ɑː² => ɑ w / _ @nasal
    # E4, E8: ɑː < a before r, and in "father" words
    ɑː => ɑ
    # Lost gh (team): ɔː before t < ME ow
    ɔː² => o w / _ t
    # E7: ɔː < ɑʊ elsewhere; E4: ɔː < ɑ before r
    ɔː² => ɑ / _ ɹ
    ɔː² => ɑ w
    # E4: ɜː < ɛ ɪ ʊ before r
    ɜː² => i
    ɜː³ => u
    ɜː => e
    # E3: yod coalescence
    tʃ² => t j
    ʃ² => s j
    dʒ² => d j
    ʒ => z j
    # E2: final mb ŋɡ > m ŋ
    m² => m b / _ $
    ŋ² => ŋ ɡ / _ $
    # E9: TRAP æ < a; E1: STRUT ʌ ɤ < ʊ; notation bridge
    æ => ɑ
    {ʌ, ɤ} => u
    {ɪ, ɛ, ʊ, a, ɹ} => {i, e, u, ɑ, r}
